export default {"id":"djing-level-7","number":7,"title":"The Digital Mixer · Gate D","skillBand":"Textbook","duration":"From the course textbook","summary":"- Track meters show peak and RMS. Internal drive into red in Live’s 32-bit float engine is not identical to clipping the physical output. Clipping matters when audio leaves Live (Main to hardware, export). Keep Main output levels appropriat","modules":[{"id":"djing-m-7-1","code":"7","title":"The Digital Mixer · Gate D","blurb":"- Track meters show peak and RMS. Internal drive into red in Live’s 32-bit float engine is not identical to clipping the physical output. Clipping matters when audio leaves Live (Main to hardware, export). Keep Main output levels appropriat","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"djing-l-o-7","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"overview","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Module 7 — The Digital Mixer · Gate D","level":1},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Objective:</strong> Integrate gain, faders, crossfader curves, EQ, filter, and the dual-bass rule as one performance system.   <strong>Difficulty:</strong> Intermediate — later transitions assume this material is automatic.   <strong>Sources:</strong> Live 12 Manual §18 Mixing (meters, headroom, crossfader seven curves, cueing); <em>How-to-DJ</em> dual-bass swap; Club Ready and related bass-swap and filter teaching; gain-staging practice from local Production_DJing gain documentation (DJ-relevant subset)."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"djing-l-7-1-1","title":"7.1.1 — Gain Structure, Faders, Meters, Crossfader Curves","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Manual points that affect practice","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Track meters show peak and RMS. Internal drive into red in Live’s 32-bit float engine is not identical to clipping the physical output. Clipping matters when audio leaves Live (Main to hardware, export). Keep Main output levels appropriate; redlining the master into converters is a performance failure (Manual §18.1).  ","Utility is the trim tool before large fader adjustments.  ","Match levels by ear and meter, not by matching fader positions on differently mastered tracks."],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Crossfader (Manual §18.5)","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Functions like a DJ crossfader but can include any number of tracks and returns.  ","Assign A, B, or none per track.  ","Seven curves (right-click): select style. Practical mapping for this course:  ","Constant Power (or smooth power-style) for long blends  ","Cut or sharp families for hard switches and cut practice  ","Crossfader affects gain stage, not routing destination — a track can still route to individual outs.  ","Channel-fader-only mixing with crossfader parked center is valid Ableton practice. Learn both methods."],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure — gain and blend laboratory","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Two warped tracks of similar energy.  ","Utility trim so each peaks in a healthy zone with channel faders near unity.  ","Practice: long blend on Constant Power; hard cut on Cut curve; channel-fader-only blend with crossfader centered.  ","Record one of each; mark gain jumps."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Common errors","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Matching fader heights instead of loudness  ","Red Main into the room to increase perceived energy  ","Wrong curve for the transition type  ","Incorrect crossfader assignment with simultaneous uncontrolled channel faders  "],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Laboratory 7.1.1","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Twelve blends: four power-curve, four cut-curve, four fader-only. Score gain continuity 0–2 each."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Pass criteria:</strong> Average at least 1.5; no intentional master clip into hardware during the laboratory."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"djing-l-7-2-1","title":"7.2.1 — EQ, Filter, Dual-Bass Rule · Gate D","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.2.1 — EQ, Filter, Dual-Bass Rule · Gate D","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Dual-bass rule","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"Two full low ends at once mud the floor. <strong>Bass swap</strong> (<em>How-to-DJ</em> / Club Ready consensus):"},{"type":"list","items":["Incoming B enters with lows reduced (EQ Three Low kill or down, or high-pass filter).  ","On a phrase boundary, swap: raise B lows while cutting A lows.  ","Finish mids and highs as the phrase continues.  ","Hard and gradual swaps are both valid — choose by genre density and drop timing (often swap on beat 1)."],"ordered":true},{"type":"heading","text":"EQ Three first","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"Default for beginners: EQ Three kills for fast performance. EQ Eight racks are advanced transparent options later and are not required for Gate D."},{"type":"heading","text":"Filter as transition control (preview of Module 9)","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"High-pass in on incoming; low-pass out on outgoing; combined swaps. Use resonance sparingly (screams and headroom). Filter motion does not excuse concurrent full low ends."},{"type":"heading","text":"High-pass on reverb return (preview)","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"Send reverb that is not high-passed smears lows across the mix. Detail is locked in Modules 9–10; begin the habit on Return A now."},{"type":"heading","text":"Gate D — self-assessment","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["[ ] Utility trim habit automatic  ","[ ] Constant Power blend and Cut switch both demonstrated  ","[ ] Bass swap on phrase boundary: at least 8 of 10 clean (no dual-bass mud)  ","[ ] Filter and swap combination once without mud  ","[ ] Recorded evidence of five bass swaps with timestamps  "],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>If criteria are not met:</strong> remain on this module. Module 9 will amplify incorrect bass habits."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Module 7 checkpoint","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["[ ] Mixer system (gain, crossfader, EQ, dual-bass rule) integrated  ","[ ] Gate D evidence recorded  "],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]}]};
